 <div class="kicker">Drum notation &middot; side by side</div>
 <h1>Our Appleseed Cast drum tabs against Songsterr&#x27;s</h1>
 <p class="lede">Five songs have both a Songsterr tab and one of our stem-built .gp5 drum parts. This is what each file actually contains, measured rather than eyeballed.</p>
 <div class="method"><b>How each number was obtained.</b> Our side is read out of the
 <code>.gp5</code> with PyGuitarPro. Their side is Songsterr's own notation JSON, fetched from
 <code>dqsljvtekg760.cloudfront.net/&lt;songId&gt;/&lt;revisionId&gt;/&lt;image&gt;/&lt;partId&gt;.json</code>, the
 path their player uses. Songsterr writes repeat barlines and we write the part out flat, so bars
 are given both as written and as played. A dash means the field does not exist on that side,
 which is different from a zero.</div>
</header>

